# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# What Pax.app bundles for the iPhone helper (v0.8.6), installed with --no-deps.
#
# pymobiledevice3's own dependency list is much larger (IPython, FastAPI, Pillow, QUIC,
# tunnels...), about 200 MB, almost all for features Pax never uses. This list is the
# import closure of the modules device/pax_device.py uses (usbmux, lockdown, exceptions,
# services.mobile_config, diagnostics, mobilebackup2, afc, notification_proxy,
# installation_proxy and springboard (v0.8.7 app picker; no new packages),
# device_link, plus cryptography for the keybag), traced with sys.platform = "darwin" so the
# macOS-only imports (ioregistry) are included. `pax_device.py selftest` imports all of
# them, and the release build runs it against the signed helper inside Pax.app, so a
# pymobiledevice3 update that needs another package fails the build, not a user's set-up.
#
# Regenerate the hashes after changing a version:
#   python3 device/lock_bundle.py            (writes device/requirements-bundle.txt)
# Every package's licence is in docs/DEPENDENCIES.md (all GPL-3.0-compatible).
pymobiledevice3==11.32.0
backports-zstd==1.8.0
bpylist2==4.1.1
certifi==2026.7.22
cffi==2.1.1
chardet==7.6.0
charset-normalizer==3.5.2
click==8.5.0
